{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nAfter the outbound child, a release the Jira project lacks (never created, deleted, renamed, or archived) is sent as a per-item add every pass; Jira answers 400 and `dispatch_one._update_one_dispatch_releases` only logs it, so nobody on the ticket sees why. The operator decided (epic comment, 2026-11-05): do not write such a name, keep it on the rebar ticket, raise a `BRIDGE_ALERT` naming it, retry each pass, never create Jira versions. ADR 0124 decisions 8 and 9 add the archived rule and the alert lifecycle.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. **Version reads.** Add `get_project_versions(project_key) -> list[dict]` (`{\"name\", \"archived\"}`) to `TicketTransport` and `_REQUIRED_TRANSPORT_MEMBERS` in `src/rebar/reconciler/_backend.py`. Cloud (`adapters/jira/acli_rest.py`): `self._direct_rest_get(f\"/rest/api/3/project/{key}/versions\")` (documented unpaginated). DC (`adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py`): `self._client.project_versions(key)` through `_call_logged`/`_unwrap`. Test transports with `add_fix_version` gain it (the 7 from the outbound child; stateful fakes return their seeded versions); `test_transport_port_completeness.py` `_REQUIRED` and the Cloud sweep's `_NON_MUTATING` list it as a READ.\n2. **Availability.** New `src/rebar/reconciler/release_alerts.py`: `read_release_availability(client, project_keys) -> dict[str, dict[str, str]]` (project → name → `\"available\"|\"archived\"`); a read error leaves that project absent = unknown. `outbound_pass._run_differs_outbound` reads it once per pass for projects (the bound key's prefix) of bound tickets that have releases or an unresolved `release-version-` alert, and passes `release_availability` plus an empty `release_withheld_sink` dict on `OutboundDiffConfig`.\n3. **Withhold.** `outbound_releases._diff_releases` takes the ticket's availability map (None = unknown, unchanged behavior). With a known map, an intended ADD of a missing or archived name becomes a withheld record `{\"release\", \"reason\": \"missing\"|\"archived\"}` instead of a Jira add; REMOVEs are unchanged. `release_mutations_for` records `sink[local_id] = (jira_key, withheld)` for every bound ticket diffed with known availability.\n4. **Keep it local.** `OutboundMutation` gains `withheld_releases: list[str]`, included in the emit condition; `inbound_differ._build_outbound_context` indexes withheld names as release adds, so the same-pass inbound REMOVE is suppressed every pass. `outbound_pass` builds no typed update when a mutation has nothing dispatchable (only withheld names).\n5. **Alerts.** `release_alerts.plan_release_alerts(ticket, withheld) -> list[dict]` is pure: a new alert `{\"reason\": \"release-version-<missing|archived>:<name>\", \"tag\": \"release-version-<missing|archived>\", \"release\": name}` per withheld name without an unresolved alert of that reason, and `{\"resolved\": true, \"resolves_uuid\": <uuid>, \"reason\": <reason>}` per unresolved `release-version-` alert whose name is no longer withheld. `release_alerts.write_release_alerts(sink, local_by_id, tracker_dir)` writes each as a `BRIDGE_ALERT` via `inbound_translate._write_event_file`; `outbound_pass` calls it after the diff, only when `ctx.persist` (preview writes nothing). The reducer already folds both shapes (`reducer/_processors.process_bridge_alert`).\n6. **Never create versions.** No code calls a version-create endpoint; the stateful fakes record every call and a test asserts none is a create.\n7. **Docs.** `docs/jira-sync-setup.md` \"Fix versions\" note: versions are created by people, never the bridge; alert names; retry; archived rule.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/`: `_backend.py`, `adapters/jira/acli_rest.py`, `adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py`, `release_alerts.py` (new), `outbound_pass.py`, `outbound_differ.py`, `outbound_releases.py`, `outbound_mutation_builders.py`, `inbound_differ.py`\n- `docs/jira-sync-setup.md`\n- New: `tests/unit/reconciler/test_release_alerts.py`\n- Extended: `tests/unit/reconciler/diffing/test_outbound_releases.py`, `mutate/test_fix_version_transport.py`, `tests/integration/reconciler/test_reconcile_releases_roundtrip.py` (seed versions), `test_transport_port_completeness.py`, `test_cloud_rate_limit_sweep.py`, and the 7 test transports (`tests/unit/reconciler/`: `backend_support.py`, `apply/_sync_only_dispatch_probe.py`, `mutate/test_coordinator_route_census.py`, `mutate/test_outbound_update_combined.py`, `orchestrate/test_e2e_dedup_pass.py`, `orchestrate/test_reconcile_once.py`; `tests/integration/reconciler/test_reconcile_idempotency.py`)\n\n## Testing\n\n- `plan_release_alerts`: withheld `2.4`, no alert → one `release-version-missing:2.4` alert; same with it unresolved → `[]`; unresolved alert for `2.4` no longer withheld → one resolution with its uuid; archived → `release-version-archived:2.4`.\n- `read_release_availability`: a raising transport leaves that project absent.\n- Diff: missing → no add, one withheld; archived likewise; available → add; REMOVE of an archived name still emitted; unknown map → add (prior behavior).\n- Transports: Cloud reads `GET /rest/api/3/project/REB/versions`; DC calls `project_versions(\"REB\")`; both map to `{\"name\",\"archived\"}`.\n- Integration (Cloud and DC backends): pass 1 with local `2.4` absent from the project writes one alert, no Jira add, and keeps `2.4` locally; pass 2 writes nothing; after the version appears, pass 3 adds it to Jira and resolves the alert; pass 4 writes nothing; an archived version gives the archived alert; a failing version read writes no alert and resolves none; no call is a version create; a preview pass writes no alert.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A release the project lacks is not written to Jira; pinned by the integration test.\n- [ ] That release stays on the rebar ticket across passes; pinned by the integration test.\n- [ ] It gets exactly one unresolved `BRIDGE_ALERT` naming it; pinned by the integration test.\n- [ ] Once the version exists, the next pass writes it and resolves the alert; pinned by the integration test.\n- [ ] An archived version is withheld with `release-version-archived:<name>`; pinned by the alert and integration tests.\n- [ ] A failed version read writes and resolves no alert; pinned by the integration test.\n- [ ] No bridge code path creates a Jira version; pinned by the fake-transport assertion.\n- [ ] `docs/jira-sync-setup.md` documents the alert, retry and version prerequisite.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` exits 0.\n  provenance: environment=macOS dev host, worktree fixver-epic at the pushed commit; principal=Rebar Bot Nava (session 3d705fec); privilege_posture=narrower; instrument=live-call — ran inside `make lint` within `make verify` on 4d21c744977; exit status is a run result, not a repository artifact\n- [ ] [non-codebase] `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exits 0.\n  provenance: environment=macOS dev host, worktree fixver-epic at the pushed commit; principal=Rebar Bot Nava (session 3d705fec); privilege_posture=narrower; instrument=live-call — ran inside `make lint` within `make verify` on 4d21c744977; exit status is a run result\n- [ ] [non-codebase] No `src/rebar` file exceeds 800 lines.\n  provenance: environment=macOS dev host, worktree fixver-epic at the pushed commit; principal=Rebar Bot Nava (session 3d705fec); privilege_posture=narrower; instrument=live-call — measured with `wc -l` over src/rebar at 4d21c744977 and enforced by the module-size gate in `make verify`\n- [ ] [non-codebase] `env -u JIRA_URL -u JIRA_USER -u JIRA_API_TOKEN make verify` exits 0 on the commit pushed for review.\n  provenance: environment=macOS dev host, worktree fixver-epic at the pushed commit; principal=Rebar Bot Nava (session 3d705fec); privilege_posture=narrower; instrument=live-call — the full local test contract run on 4d21c744977; its exit status and log exist only outside the repository"}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794391815770468270,"uuid":"dcd532fc-50d2-4d43-aa83-af31acde3456"}